misc: fastrpc: allocate the sensors domain's messages from the reserved pool

From the OnePlus 7T Pro port (Robin Snyders, hotdog-linux-bringup, 0148), less
its per-invoke dev_info trace, which filled 98% of the log there. The sensors
protection domain does not reach the message buffer through its SMMU context
bank: given a mapped buffer it addressed memory that was not there, first
faulting on the session id folded into the upper bits and, once that was
corrected, stalling the interconnect until the watchdog reset the SoC.

--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -954,7 +954,13 @@
 
 	ctx->msg_sz = pkt_size;
 
-	if (ctx->fl->sctx->sid)
+	/*
+	 * The sensors domain reaches the message buffer directly rather than
+	 * through its context bank, so it needs one from the reserved pool.
+	 * A context-bank mapping leaves it addressing memory that is not
+	 * there, which stalls the interconnect rather than faulting.
+	 */
+	if (ctx->fl->sctx->sid && ctx->fl->pd != SENSORS_PD)
 		err = fastrpc_buf_alloc(ctx->fl, dev, pkt_size, &ctx->buf);
 	else
 		err = fastrpc_remote_heap_alloc(ctx->fl, dev, pkt_size, &ctx->buf);
